{
 "schema_version": 1,
 "note": [
  "Step 6 of 2.0: the layout matrix. Python (tests/contracts/test_layout_matrix.py) and Rust",
  "(rust/crates/pcbridge-core/tests/layout_matrix.rs) resolve every state with their own",
  "production resolver and must produce this table. Expected values were computed by hand:",
  "canvas size = mode / scale in the logical layout mode and = mode in the physical mode,",
  "axes swapped for transforms 1/3/5/7, canvas moved to start at (0, 0), numbered by (x, y).",
  "`scaled` is the picture size at the default long edge 1536 and area cap 1536x864;",
  "`legible` says whether small text keeps at least half its size (shown share x UI scale).",
  "`gaps` are canvas points inside the bounding box that lie on no monitor.",
  "Only the two-1080p layout is measured hardware; this machine runs the physical mode",
  "(layout-mode 2, measured 2026-09-23)."
 ],
